(* q-reach.pvl
   The queries of the session models that say the models do something (AUD-5, #389; AUD-6, #409; see
   docs/formal-model.md for how formal.py reads a query: each is one statement with its id in the comment before it). The
   queries of a group are joined to a model by variants.tsv, and expected.tsv says what each must give in it. *)

(* The server can take a session as the one of alice (her Login, her Hello, or her session as a peer) and the client can
   complete the handshake, so that no query that holds is true only because nothing happens. A variant in which the
   handshake cannot complete expects them to hold, which says that it cannot. *)
(* @query reach-took *)
query t: bitstring; event(ServerTook(bob, alice, t)).
(* @query reach-done *)
query t: bitstring, h: bitstring; event(ClientDone(alice, bob, t, h)).
